{"step_index":578,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T17:32:27Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Duplicates**\n\nOkay, I'm now zeroing in on the duplication of \"Thông tin khác\" in the UI. I'm trying to figure out the root cause of the repeating label. My main focus is on the data binding mechanism and conditional rendering logic within the UI component. I suspect there might be a loop or an error in how the data is being fetched and displayed.\n\n\n**Investigating the Data**\n\nI've been looking deeper into the data structure, particularly focusing on how \"Thông tin khác\" is handled. I am analyzing the string manipulation logic in `src/app/(portal)/kts/hien-trang/page.tsx`, specifically the way newlines are treated. It seems that newlines within the original Excel cells are causing the \"other info\" section to split inappropriately, which is likely the root cause of the issue. The newlines seem to be contributing to the splitting of the information.\n\n\n**Refining the Delimiter**\n\nI've realized the core issue stems from how Excel newlines are being imported as literal newlines, leading to incorrect splitting. The code currently splits at both `\\\\n` and `\\n`, causing individual bullet points within a cell to be treated as separate attributes. My plan now is to adjust the parsing logic in `hien-trang/page.tsx`. Specifically, I will modify it to recognize that lines without the `::` prefix are continuations of the preceding attribute's value. Alternatively, changing the delimiter is also a possibility.\n\n\n**Fixing the Delimiter**\n\nI've realized the problem is still the escaped `\\\\n` delimiter inserted into the database. I was using `\\\\n` to join the parts of the description in `import_snn.js`, meaning the database stores literal backslash-n characters. I must change the delimiter to `\\n` in `import_snn.js` to store actual newline characters, and modify the UI to parse these newlines as intended. I'm focusi